Welcome to the MagnetDB duckdb demonstrator development environment!

Base image: debian:trixie (no MagnetTools: hoop-stress commands unavailable)

Available tools:
  - Python with scientific computing libraries
  - Jupyter notebooks (Voila on port 8866)

Workspace: /workspaces/magnetdb-duckdb-demo
Datasets:  /mnt/LNCMIG-Data/records  (host: ~/magnetdb-duckdb-data/records)
DuckDB:    /data/duckdb              (host: ~/magnetdb-duckdb-data/duckdb)
CSV data:  /workspaces/magnetdb-duckdb-demo/Data  (repo Data/, not in git)
           SUPERVISION: Data/bdd.csv

Data needed (ask LNCMI staff for it):
  - Data-csv.tgz      -> repo root:            tar -xzf Data-csv.tgz
                         (CSV data incl. SUPERVISION Data/bdd.csv)
  - <name>.duckdb     -> host ~/magnetdb-duckdb-data/duckdb   (/data/duckdb here)
  - <magnet>.tar.xz   -> host ~/magnetdb-duckdb-data/records  (/mnt/LNCMIG-Data/records here)
                         tar -xJf <magnet>.tar.xz -C ~/magnetdb-duckdb-data/records
Files added later appear here immediately, no rebuild needed.

!!! Do not forget to start the python virtualenv !!!:
source /home/myuser/.venvs/magnetdb/bin/activate
(Debian python3, isolated venv: no system site-packages)

The workspace .venv belongs to the host: do not use it here.
